    {
        "id": "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h3",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h2"
        ],
        "title": "The period",
        "text": "The period of $$\\tan(\\theta)$$ is $$\\pi.$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h4",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h3"
        ],
        "title": "Interpreting the period",
        "text": "If $$\\tan(\\theta)=y,$$ then $$\\tan(\\theta+n\\pi)=y$$ for any integer $$n.$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h5",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h4"
        ],
        "title": "Shift the principal value into the desired interval",
        "text": "To find the equivalent angle in the required physical range of $$[\\pi, 2\\pi], $$ we add the period $$\\pi$$ to our principal value of $$\\frac{\\pi}{4}.$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h6",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h5"
        ],
        "title": "Visualize the equivalent angle",
        "text": "Due to the fact that the tangent has period $$\\pi, $$ $$\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\pi=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}.$$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "",
        "license": ""
    },
    {
        "id": "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h7",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": [
            "ac048eeT331-trigcancel-P04a-h6"
        ],
        "title": "Visualize the equivalent angle",
        "text": "Visually, tangent represents the slope of the line at an angle. If we draw a line through the origin and $$\\frac{\\pi}{4}, $$ it intersects the other side of the unit circle at $$\\frac{5\\pi}{4}.$$ Thus both of these angles have the same tangent.\\n##figure1.gif##",
